  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting your log home ready for a new finish is super important; it’s all about creating a clean, dry canvas for the best results. Here’s a quick run-down of the process. First, you need to evaluate the current coating and its condition. This will help you decide if you just need a good cleaning or if stripping is necessary. Sometimes, if the old finish is really failing or incompatible, stripping is the way to go. Next, you'll either clean or strip the surface. Many experts suggest dry removal methods, like corn blasting, over pressure washing because blasting won’t force excess water into the wood fibers. You really want to avoid trapping moisture under your new finish! After cleaning or stripping, it's crucial to let the wood completely dry out. This can take some time, so don't rush it. Once the logs are dry, you can apply a compatible log-home specific stain or clear finish. It's really important to use products designed for log homes to ensure breathability and proper protection. And finally, remember that maintenance is ongoing; periodic reapplication will keep your logs looking great and protected for years to come. If you're tackling a big project in the greater Denver area and need a hand, give HH Remodeling LLC a call!"
    }
  ],
